worked on — note staged modifications), `lib/run.sh`, `lib/loops.sh` and all `lib/loops/*.sh`, `lib/agent.sh`, `lib/worker.sh`, `lib/loop-launcher.sh`. Skim providers and harden-core.\n\nLook at:\n- `cmd/*.sh` — CLI entry points, list/sync/install/hub\n- `tests/*.sh` — how tests reach behaviour. Are they unit-testing pure helpers when bugs live in callers?\n\nReport 5-10 specific friction findings with file:line refs. For each: which module, what is shallow/leaky/duplicated/etc, and why deleting/restructuring would concentrate complexity. Use the CONTEXT.md vocabulary (module/seam/adapter/depth/leverage/locality). Don't propose solutions — just identify friction. Under 1000 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5371,"cache_read_input_tokens":37076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5371},"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a7c94be-b519-4ed0-b07c-6b329c049eda","uuid":"34bef9a7-a84f-49d6-ae70-68ebf6d2ae38","request_id":"req_011CbShAFnF2SUfm1KaA35cD"}
