{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VzbKQUE4Vaidpkc2213ULN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've explored the codebase. Prior converge runs have polished this heavily — the most recent goal was literally \"the skill almanac:codebase-improve doesn't give any substantial improvements to do.\" Honest candidates:\n\n**Candidates surfaced**\n\n1. **Feedback marker→command vs command→description coupling** (`lib/feedback.sh`)\n   - **Problem**: `almanac_loop_feedback_commands()` emits commands per marker; `almanac_loop_feedback_command_description()` holds a parallel `case` mapping each command to text. Add a command in one without the other → markdown silently degrades to \"run feedback loop\". No single source of truth.\n   - **Solution**: collapse to one private rows function emitting `cmd\\tdesc` per marker; derive both public functions from it.\n   - **Benefit**: locality — one place to add markers. Deletion test passes: removing the rows function would force re-introducing the parallel map.\n\n2. **Adapter discovery duplication** (`lib/loops.sh` + `lib/agent.sh`)\n   - **Problem**: Both seams hand-roll identical `*_key`/`*_load`/`*_list`/`*_known`/`*_call` (~30 lines each).\n   - **Solution**: extract generic registry helpers; each seam keeps its own `*_key` (claude-code normalisation differs).\n   - **Verdict**: marginal — the dedup is small, bash indirection adds friction, and the two seams already test independently. Declining unless the user wants it.\n\nOther findings from the Explore agent (argv globals, worker health, converge parser, TSV record engine, role layering, hub control, harden ledger) all turn out to be deliberate deep designs documented in `CONTEXT.md` or already deep (e.g., `worker_health` is a pure predicate + composer pair). Not worth re-litigating.\n\nProceeding with C1 (feedback rows). C2 declined as marginal."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,